            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 694)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Compare pairs, set up in the playlist.</b> A pair is two clips and how they are shown together &#8212; saved with the session, so a review can be organized before the meeting. Press <b>Pair for Compare</b> under the playlist and tick two clips (the first is A), or hold a row&#8217;s compare button and choose Compare with. New pairs are shown side by side.</li>
<li><b>Arriving on a pair shows it</b> in its mode, with no keypress, and playback treats it as one stop &#8212; B is already on screen, so next/previous pass over it. Tick &#8220;B is also a stop&#8221; when B needs its own notes.</li>
<li><b>One compare button per row</b> replaces the A chip, the B chip and the split icon. On a pair: click for on/off, hold to choose Side by Side, Stacked, Wipe, Difference, Over or Add. Change the mode or the wipe while a pair is on screen and the pair remembers it.</li>
<li>Pairs travel to web reviews: they show in the web playlist, and a guest browsing on their own arrives on a pair in its compare. Sessions saved with the old A and B chips open with those marks read as pairs.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
